WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.279
Avengers: Infinity War is an event of cosmic
significance, both in our world, and in the

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:06.880
Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.080
For us, it's one of the biggest blockbusters
of all time, an unprecedented culmination

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.610
of 10 years and 18 movies leading up to a
gigantic finale.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:19.360
But for the characters of the MCU, Infinity
War looks primed to be their bleakest outing

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.450
yet, and with the release of its massive first
trailer, many fans are increasingly starting

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.130
to fear that some of these characters may
not be around for much longer.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.340
The biggest potential candidate on the chopping
block is also the most powerful member of

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.650
the team: Paul Bettany's synthetic life form,
Vision.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:38.990
Key to the theory of Vision's impending demise
is the fact that the exact thing that gave

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:43.410
Vision life in Avengers: Age of Ultron—his
forehead-embedded Mind Stone—is one of the

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:48.020
six powerful Infinity Stones Thanos has spent
the last decade plotting his way across the

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.020
universe to acquire.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:50.690
"You know I don't know what this is?

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.420
I know it's not of this world.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:58.329
It powered Loki's staff and it gave you your
abilities, but its true nature is a mystery."

00:00:58.329 --> 00:01:03.899
"Before creation itself, there were six singularities.

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:13.940
And the remnants of these systems were forged
into concentrated ingots, Infinity Stones."

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.810
One shot in the trailer has Vision sprawled
on the ground in evident defeat, having his

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:22.330
forehead violently probed by one of Thanos'
allies, which suggests that Thanos is going

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:26.390
to get his hands on the stone—and if this
doesn't end Vision's life outright, he probably

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.400
won't last long against Thanos and his horde
without his powers.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.180
In a storytelling sense, it would make sense
to take Vision out of commission for the big

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.180
Thanos fight.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:38.590
The Vision is immensely powerful, so much
so that the movies have pointedly neglected

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:42.340
to use him during certain battle scenes, in
a similar fashion to the way they've sometimes

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:43.980
sidelined the Hulk.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:48.510
Vision's new, more human form and his romance
with Scarlet Witch also raises suspicions

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.050
that the end is near for him.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.740
It's a classic move: they remind you why you
love the character, and then they stick the

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:54.740
knife in.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:55.580
Sometimes literally.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.960
Honestly, it wouldn't be a surprise if many
of Marvel's heroes met their ends in shocking

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.429
ways in Infinity War.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:13.400
Beyond the actors' expiring contracts, and
the fact that the team's mass extinction was

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:17.969
already teased in Avengers: Age of Ultron,
Marvel Studios' head Kevin Feige has been

00:02:17.969 --> 00:02:22.470
vocal in his belief that the studio needs
to move forward with new characters and new

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.470
ideas.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:24.470
He told Vanity Fair,

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:27.760
"If Marvel is going to survive, they have
to start making movies with characters who

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:28.939
are a little different.

00:02:28.939 --> 00:02:31.150
They have to start allowing characters to
die."

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:34.400
It increasingly looks like that time of reckoning
is now.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.469
Not only have the movies been building to
a fatal conclusion with the mad titan Thanos,

00:02:38.469 --> 00:02:42.260
the comics on which the story is based saw
Thanos getting away with lots and lots of

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.030
murder of some very recognizable names—at
least, for a while.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:50.230
In Marvel's The Infinity Gauntlet miniseries,
Thanos used the unprecedented power of the

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:54.669
collected Infinity Stones, which are called
"Infinity Gems" in the comics, to effortlessly

00:02:54.669 --> 00:02:58.959
blink half of all living creatures in the
universe out of existence, including heroes

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:01.489
like the Fantastic Four and several Avengers.

00:03:01.489 --> 00:03:05.510
And when the surviving heroes confronted him,
he pretty much wrecked all of them, too.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:09.549
With that comic book history in mind, could
this be what Infinity War is building to?

00:03:09.549 --> 00:03:13.609
It was previously said that the subtitle for
the fourth Avengers movie hasn't been released

00:03:13.609 --> 00:03:17.730
because it is in itself a spoiler—does the
title refer to the Avengers' defeat?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.540
Is Disney pulling an Empire Strikes Back on
us, where all the heroes get their butts kicked?

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.689
Was Mark Ruffalo telling the truth after all?

00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:27.120
"Wait until you see this next one - EVERYBODY
DIES."

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:27.800
"DUDE!

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:28.800
DUDE!"

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:29.840
Well—maybe.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.650
We'll know for sure when Avengers: Infinity
War finally hits theaters on May 4, 2018.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:35.989
Can you even stand it?!

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:36.989
Thanks for watching!

00:03:36.989 --> 00:03:39.069
